11855	{"artifactId":"HLD-613abdb351c2c738","entry":{"id":"migrated-HLD-613abdb351c2c738-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-14T08:53:09.074Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"pass","summary":"review: pass","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.epic","stage":"design.epic","verdict":"pass","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Every DEF functional requirement (FR001–FR008 and the S001–S005 story FRs) is designed in some Story boundary or shared contract, including S004:FR003 (Stop leaves a failed message with a resend) and S005:FR004 (attachments of waiting/failed messages are kept).","evidence":"DEF.md:28-70 lists FR001–FR008 and the story FRs. The HLD maps them as follows. FR001/S001 → sc1/sc4 with head() and acknowledge(). FR002/S002 → sc5 OutboxView, with processing rows dropped per S002:FR002. FR003 → the SQLite rows survive a reload. FR004 → cancel/dismiss/resend. FR005/S003 → takeOver after LEASE_TAKEOVER_MS=600_000 with the process checks. FR006/S004 → retries at 10 s, 1 min and 5 min, at most 3, gated on 'acted'. FR007/S005 → submit with origin 'review-pane'. FR008 → QUEUE_RECORD_BOUND=500 with a 'full' refusal. S004:FR003 → TurnOutcome 'stopped' becomes failed with 'stopped by the user'. S005:FR004 → liveSessionIds() feeds the sweep keep set and the eviction keep predicate. [files: docs/epics/per-repo-chat-turn-queue-outbox-E20261014613abdb3/DEF.md]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"No non-goal is built: nothing runs a turn again by itself other than the bounded infra retries before the turn acted, and there is no leader/dispatcher window.","evidence":"DEF.md:78 names the non-goal 'Running a message unattended or running a turn again by itself, other than the bounded retries...'. In the HLD, a dead window's processing message is marked failed (S003), not re-run. The retry is gated on `acted: false`. a3 (the dispatcher) is rejected for leaning towards the leader-window design. [files: docs/epics/per-repo-chat-turn-queue-outbox-E20261014613abdb3/DEF.md]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"turn-lifecycle.start() supersedes the previous turn (newest wins), and detach() keeps a session-file turn running but stops a pipe turn as stop() does (turn-lifecycle.ts:511-525).","evidence":"turn-lifecycle.ts:243-248: 'Single-in-flight: the newest message wins. A turn still waiting for the lock is dropped' with `waitCtl?.abort(); const myGen = ++generation;`. At :517-525, `if (detachThis !== undefined && liveProc?.cursor !== undefined) { ... detachThis(); return; } await stopLive();`, so a turn without a cursor (a pipe turn) is stopped. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/turn-lifecycle.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The session lock's liveness check prefers the CLI pid over the host pid (session-lock.ts:397), using process.kill(pid, 0) (:294).","evidence":"session-lock.ts:397: `rec.cliPid !== null ? isAlive(rec.cliPid) && sameProcess(rec) : isAlive(rec.hostPid);` and :294: `process.kill(pid, 0);`. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/session-lock.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.3","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The chat's working folder is the first workspace folder, falling back to process.cwd(). The review pane hands over via chatHost.submitExternal at extension.ts:712.","evidence":"extension.ts:481: `const chatCwd = (): string => vscode.workspace.workspaceFolders?.[0]?.uri.fsPath ?? process.cwd();` and extension.ts:712: `notifyChat: (text) => chatHost.submitExternal(text),`. [files: vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"AttachmentRef is reused as is, with the shape { id, name, kind, size, path }.","evidence":"attachment-store.ts:23-32: `export interface AttachmentRef { readonly id: string; readonly name: string; readonly kind: 'image' | 'file'; readonly size: number; readonly path: string; }`. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/attachment-store.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"No cross-window store and no existing infrastructure-error classification exist in the plugin, so the SQLite queue and the InfraCause classification are genuinely new.","evidence":"A grep for isTransientCliError in vscode-plugin/src finds nothing, and the plugin has no node:sqlite import (c2). The only cross-window coordination is the per-session lock files in session-lock.ts. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/session-lock.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Every runTurn caller and supersede site is listed: the grant re-run :578, the selection continuation :1671, the submit sites :1432/:1439 and :1506/:1507, drainExternal :697-703, and submitExternal :1825-1831.","evidence":"A grep of chat-panel.ts finds runTurn( at 578, 703, 1439, 1507 and 1671. supersedeQueuedApprovals() is called at 702, 1432 and 1506. waitingExternal is at 177 and submitExternal returns 'queued' or 'sent' at 1831. These match the HLD's inventory, including drainExternal's call at :702 going with s5. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The review-pane result type change sites are complete: ExternalSubmitResult (chat-panel.ts:154), notifyChat (docs-review-panel.ts:45), ChatHandOver (:65), decisionResultLine 'sent' (:2452), and the test default 'sent' (docs-review-decision.test.ts:126).","evidence":"chat-panel.ts:154: `export type ExternalSubmitResult = 'sent' | 'queued' | 'unavailable';`. docs-review-panel.ts:45: `notifyChat?: ((text: string) => 'sent' | 'queued' | 'unavailable')`. :65: `type ChatHandOver = 'sent' | 'queued' | 'unavailable' | 'failed' | 'none';`. :2452: `case 'sent': parts.push('The chat has been told.')`. docs-review-decision.test.ts:126 returns 'sent'. chat-panel.test.ts:4951 and :4961 assert 'sent'. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/docs-review-panel.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/docs-review-decision.test.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.3","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Session eviction lives in session-file-store.ts evictBeyondCap (:285-313), where onEvict runs after removal and cannot veto it, so a keep predicate dependency is needed on FileStoreDeps (:98-105).","evidence":"session-file-store.ts:297-308 removes the head and rows files, then calls `deps.onEvict?.(head.id)` inside a try with the comment 'eviction itself has happened'. The only exclusion today is keepId (:295). FileStoreDeps is at :98 with onEvict at :105. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/session-file-store.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Older records and mixed versions are handled. The store records its schema version and creating plugin version and migrates a newer schema in one transaction on open. Existing chat sessions and liveTurn cursors are unchanged. engines.vscode is raised from the current ^1.75.0.","evidence":"package.json:22-23 currently reads `\"engines\": { \"vscode\": \"^1.75.0\" }`, which the HLD's 'minimum VS Code version rises (k5)' addresses. The HLD's §7 Durability states the schema-version migration. The §6.1 mixed-plugin-versions note states that an un-reloaded old window starts turns outside the queue until VS Code's reload prompt is followed. No existing stored shape (session head/rows, liveTurn) is altered. [files: vscode-plugin/package.json]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Story ownership matches the DEF: S005 owns the attachment keep and eviction (DEF S005:FR004), and the phase order follows the DEF's dependsOn edges (s2, s3 → s1; s4, s5 → s1, s2). No Story redesigns a contract owned by another.","evidence":"DEF.md:70 assigns 'Images and files attached to any waiting or failed message are kept…' to S005:FR004. DEF.md:123, :138, :154 and :170 give Depends on `s1`, `s1`, `s1, s2` and `s1, s2`. The HLD's sc1-sc4 are owned by s1 and sc5 by s2, and the other Stories only consume them. [files: docs/epics/per-repo-chat-turn-queue-outbox-E20261014613abdb3/DEF.md]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each failure is detectable and its handling is stated. The cases covered are: node:sqlite missing, store busy or full, a dead window, a window whose CLI survived a reload, a pipe turn detached, an unanswered card, a deleted session, and an auth failure.","evidence":"The HLD gives a handling for each case. A missing node:sqlite reports 'unsupported VS Code' through the injected factory. EnqueueResult carries reason 'full' | 'busy' | 'unavailable' with a note (S004:FR004 and FR008). takeOver requires a stale lease and both pids gone (consistent with session-lock.ts:397), and reclaim() handles a reloaded window. A pipe turn resolves 'stopped' (verified against turn-lifecycle.ts:525). An unanswered card is bounded by CONTINUATION_WAIT_MS. A missing session fails with 'the chat no longer exists'. An auth failure is InfraCause 'auth' and leaves the message failed per S004:FR003. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/turn-lifecycle.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/session-lock.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The HLD identifies the tests that its behaviour change breaks and the new race test. The existing tests pinning newest-wins exist at the cited sites.","evidence":"turn-lifecycle.test.ts:205 is `test('a second start drops a turn still waiting for its lease'`. chat-panel.test.ts:138 is 'single-in-flight: a second submit supersedes the first' and :2854 is 'Stop ends the running process at once and cancels a waiting message'. These match the HLD's list. The risk table adds a two-process test asserting a message is acknowledged exactly once. The per-AC test mapping is left to each Story's LLD, as befits an HLD. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/turn-lifecycle.test.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":14,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-14T08:53:09.074Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
